  "description": "AJUWUB crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3 c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C270 H222 Dy16 N26 O92 P16 12-,12(K1 1+),8(C3 H7 N1 O1),4(C2 H3 N1),8(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy12 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy13 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy14 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy15 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy16 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 16 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.828-4.441 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.69-132.18°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C302H304Dy16K12N38O108P16.",
